{"format":"edopsys-canonical-source-bundle-v1","files":[{"path":"CANONICAL-SERIALIZATION.md","sha256":"f240c89a549ecf082b50a2d633c5b59ba2ec6f8392f4f06c3ede7049fd10f7ff","content":"# CLP-001 Canonical Serialization + SHA-256 Contract\n\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe governance kernel hashes semantic JSON values, not platform-specific object memory.\n\n## Canonicalization rules\n1. Inputs MUST be JSON-compatible values.\n2. Object keys are sorted lexicographically by Unicode code-unit order at every depth.\n3. Arrays preserve their original order.\n4. `undefined` object properties are omitted.\n5. `null`, booleans, strings, and finite numbers retain JSON semantics.\n6. NaN, positive infinity, and negative infinity are rejected.\n7. No insignificant whitespace is emitted.\n8. The canonical serialization is UTF-8 JSON text.\n9. SHA-256 is computed over the UTF-8 bytes of the canonical serialization.\n10. Hashes are represented as lowercase hex prefixed with `sha256:`.\n\n## DomainEvent hashing\nA runtime DomainEvent hash MUST be derived from a hash payload that excludes its own `event_hash` field. Implementations integrating the schema SHALL define that payload explicitly and freeze it before production use.\n\n## EvidenceArtifact hashing\nBUILD-CLP-001-B currently hashes the immutable evidence payload:\n- evidence_id\n- evidence_class\n- evidence_type\n- content\n- parent_evidence_ids\n\nOperational metadata that may change by workflow (for example verification metadata) is not silently included in the immutable content digest.\n\n## Cross-implementation requirement\nA conforming implementation in another language MUST produce byte-identical canonical JSON and identical SHA-256 results for the same fixture values before it may claim replay compatibility.\n"},{"path":"README.md","sha256":"5603dc0d33a9a9ae32b7d9c06b70b521d9d35de58d120192f86fbfdfad9275e7","content":"# BUILD-CLP-001-B — Deterministic Guard Engine + Replay Skeleton\n\nParent artifacts:\n- KAP-001 v1.0.0\n- CLP-001 v1.0.0\n- BUILD-CLP-001-A v1.0.0 (consumed unchanged)\n\n## Scope\nPure deterministic TypeScript governance kernel. No UI, API framework, database, network access, payment behavior, or business-feature layer.\n\n## Implemented kernel primitives\n- deterministic transition authorization against the frozen A transition policy\n- exact +1 aggregate event-version validation\n- deterministic WORKER-A/B/C eligibility evaluation\n- AI-non-override boundary for eligibility\n- append-only evidence creation and parent-lineage requirement\n- canonical JSON serialization + SHA-256 content hashing\n- evidence tamper detection\n- authority-provenance shape checks\n- jurisdiction/applicability guard behavior used by CLP-001 fixtures\n- rights-answer citation and legal-liability guard\n- WorkOrder provenance guard\n- Task Pack status/hash/version guard\n- CLP-001 stop-condition classification\n- completion-vs-verification separation\n- independent verifier enforcement\n- WorkGraph issuance gate and privacy projection\n- lineage-reference validation\n- correlation-ID historical replay skeleton with pinned versions\n\n## Verification\nRun:\n\n```bash\nnpm test\nnode scripts/verify-guardrails.mjs\n```\n\nExpected result:\n- 37 executable behavior tests PASS\n- AT-001 through AT-030 represented\n- ADV-001 through ADV-007 represented\n- BUILD-CLP-001-A manifest validates against the consumed copy\n- WORKER-A/B/C fixture outcomes match the freeze\n\n## Non-claims\nThis bundle does not claim:\n- production legal-source validation;\n- a signed remote Git commit;\n- production cryptographic signatures;\n- persistence durability;\n- authorization middleware;\n- a UI or application service.\n\nThe freeze receipt therefore records a verified source-tree digest and leaves `implementation_commit_sha` explicitly pending repository binding.\n"},{"path":"REPLAY-SPEC.md","sha256":"b96710c205cf2f7e63a02a8f64382bdc502b965564ce264b9dcd781284e85d17","content":"# CLP-001 Historical Replay Skeleton\n\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\n## Input\n`correlation_id`\n\n## Required stores\n- append-only DomainEvent records\n- referenced EvidenceArtifact records\n- immutable version registry keyed by explicit version reference (for example `AUTH@1`, `POL@1`)\n\n## Algorithm\n1. Select only events matching the requested correlation ID.\n2. Reject an empty selection.\n3. Preserve persisted event order.\n4. Verify aggregate versions progress exactly +1 within each aggregate.\n5. Verify each non-null `causation_event_id` resolves inside the replay event set.\n6. Resolve only version refs explicitly pinned by the historical events.\n7. Reject any unresolved pinned version ref.\n8. Resolve every evidence reference; reject missing evidence.\n9. Return the historical event sequence plus the exact pinned versions.\n\n## Prohibitions\nReplay MUST NOT:\n- fetch the latest authority version as a substitute;\n- substitute current policy for historical policy;\n- recalculate historical eligibility from current credentials;\n- regenerate historical AI outputs and treat them as the original artifact;\n- mutate the event stream during replay.\n\n## Current skeleton boundary\nBUILD-CLP-001-B proves version pinning, causation presence, evidence presence, and aggregate sequence integrity. Full certification replay remains a later layer because the A-bundle does not yet contain full production-shaped AuthoritySource, TaskPack, Verification, or WorkGraph fixture objects.\n"},{"path":"package.json","sha256":"8168305b3dc35f9240833b31555850d5de7c305818d26159deffc1848c9a9459","content":"{\n  \"name\": \"build-clp-001-b\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"build\": \"tsc -p tsconfig.json\",\n    \"test\": \"npm run build && node --test tests/*.test.mjs\"\n  }\n}\n"},{"path":"receipts/BUILD-CLP-001-A-freeze-receipt.json","sha256":"44ba9c56c5a471452a443e7c600c437302c944e2787e63bb54049d444cae4a52","content":"{\n  \"receipt_id\": \"BUILD-CLP-001-A-FREEZE-